        "y2": 934.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.927448034286499,
      "reading_order": 5,
      "text": "4. K has the least density among the given ele-\nments. Density decreases down the group and\nincreases across a period.\n\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_005",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 235.0,
        "y1": 956.0,
        "x2": 1174.0,
        "y2": 1138.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9180558919906616,
      "reading_order": 6,
      "text": "5. Electropositivity is pertinent to the tendency of\nan element to lose an electron.\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_006",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 236.0,
        "y1": 1160.0,
        "x2": 1080.0,
        "y2": 1488.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9247446060180664,
      "reading_order": 7,
      "text": "6. Atomic number 13 $\\rightarrow$ 2, 8, 3; group is 13.\nAtomic number 20 $\\rightarrow$ 2, 8, 8, 2; group is 2.\nAtomic number 6 $\\rightarrow$ 2, 4; group is 14.\nAtomic number 14 $\\rightarrow$ 2, 8, 4; group is 14.\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_007",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 233.0,
        "y1": 1508.0,
        "x2": 1076.0,
        "y2": 1900.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9193564057350159,
      "reading_order": 8,
      "text": "7. Atomic number: 7 $\\rightarrow$ 2, 5\nAtomic number: 3 $\\rightarrow$ 2, 1\nAtomic number: 9 $\\rightarrow$ 2, 7\nAtomic number: 11 $\\rightarrow$ 2, 8, 1\nDecreasing order of atomic size is DBAC.\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_008",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 234.0,
        "y1": 1923.0,
        "x2": 1171.0,
        "y2": 2105.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.910906970500946,
      "reading_order": 9,
      "text": "8. Since K has the largest size among the given\nelements, its ionization energy is the least.\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_009",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 234.0,
        "y1": 2127.0,
        "x2": 1174.0,
        "y2": 2363.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9091030955314636,
      "reading_order": 10,
      "text": "9. Elements with greater electron affinity can take\naway electrons from other elements and thus\nthe other elements undergo oxidation.\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_010",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1266.0,
        "y1": 290.0,
        "x2": 2218.0,
        "y2": 473.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9105920791625977,
      "reading_order": 11,
      "text": "10. Non-metallic character of an element is directly\nproportional to the electronegativity.\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_011",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1265.0,
        "y1": 509.0,
        "x2": 2222.0,
        "y2": 839.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.8053396344184875,
      "reading_order": 12,
      "text": "11. Sodium has only one valence electron. Hence,\nit becomes stable after losing one electron.\nTherefore, the value of 2nd ionization poten-\ntial increases drastically. Hence, the difference\nbetween the second and the first ionization\nenergies is the maximum."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_012",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1340.0,
        "y1": 858.0,
        "x2": 1934.0,
        "y2": 914.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.3586673438549042,
      "reading_order": 13,
      "text": "Hence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_013",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1264.0,
        "y1": 944.0,
