        "y2": 1283.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.7199071645736694,
      "reading_order": 14,
      "text": "12. They are isoelectronic with 10 electrons in\ntheir atoms. $\\mathrm{O}^{-2}$ has the largest radius since\nthe number of protons in it is the least. That is,\nthe effective nuclear force of attraction on the\nvalence electrons is less.\n\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_5_block_014",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1263.0,
        "y1": 1328.0,
        "x2": 2220.0,
        "y2": 1574.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.8754183650016785,
      "reading_order": 15,
      "text": "13. Reducing character is the tendency to undergo\noxidation and is directly proportional to the\ntendency to lose electrons.\n\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
    },
